$ plumber config resolve --help
exit: 0
--- stdout
Resolve extends and includePlumberDefaults and print the complete
effective .plumber.yaml. Use this to materialize a sparse overlay into a
full, self-contained config you can commit (nothing left implicit), or to
audit exactly what a scan will use.

Examples:
  plumber config resolve
  plumber config resolve -c overlay.yaml -o full.plumber.yaml

Usage:
  plumber config resolve [flags]

Flags:
  -c, --config string   Path to configuration file (default ".plumber.yaml")
  -h, --help            help for resolve
  -o, --output string   Write resolved config to this file (default: stdout)

Global Flags:
  -v, --verbose   Enable debug logging on stderr (level=debug); replaces the progress bar

--- stderr

